      "updated": 1,
      "text": "HOW EACH LANE REACHES THE MODEL — AND WHY D AND E COLLECT OUT OF BAND",
      "fontSize": 18,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "HOW EACH LANE REACHES THE MODEL — AND WHY D AND E COLLECT OUT OF BAND",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": false
    },
    {
      "angle": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "strokeColor": "#1b1b1b",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": null,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "type": "text",
      "id": "b_70",
      "x": 44,
      "y": 1256,
      "width": 2136,
      "height": 156,
      "seed": 555330,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 17215230,
      "updated": 1,
      "text": "Lane D — named knowledge lives in each environment; application users collect it into one tenant-wide Dataverse table.\nLane E — SharePointAgentLogging reconstructs observed .agent inventory from sharePointFileOperation audit records.\nPower BI reads those two landing-table lanes from Dataverse; it never calls their POST-only or tenant-fan-out collection paths.\nLane F — Defender advanced hunting uses one fixed host, so Power BI queries it directly at refresh time and fails soft when unavailable.\nUsage, value and cost (Copilot Chat, Cowork, per-agent conversations, credits) live in Analytics Hub, not here.\nBoth PBIP builds contain the same pages and tables: pbip-cloud reads live services; pbip reads equivalent CSV shapes, including DimSharePointAgent.",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Lane D — named knowledge lives in each environment; application users collect it into one tenant-wide Dataverse table.\nLane E — SharePointAgentLogging reconstructs observed .agent inventory from sharePointFileOperation audit records.\nPower BI reads those two landing-table lanes from Dataverse; it never calls their POST-only or tenant-fan-out collection paths.\nLane F — Defender advanced hunting uses one fixed host, so Power BI queries it directly at refresh time and fails soft when unavailable.\nUsage, value and cost (Copilot Chat, Cowork, per-agent conversations, credits) live in Analytics Hub, not here.\nBoth PBIP builds contain the same pages and tables: pbip-cloud reads live services; pbip reads equivalent CSV shapes, including DimSharePointAgent.",
      "lineHeight": 2,
      "autoResize": false
    }
  ],
